          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.113,
            0.847,
            0.169
          ],
          "content": "1. The population of Bengaluru in 2025 is about 250% of its population in 2000. If the population in 2000 was 50 lakhs, what is the population in 2025?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.179,
            0.847,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": "2. The population of the world in 2025 is about 8.2 billion. The populations of some countries in 2025 are given. Match them with their approximate percentage share of the worldwide population. [**Hint:** Writing these numbers in the standard form and estimating can help]."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.216,
            0.292,
            0.312,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": "Germany 83 million"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.369,
            0.292,
            0.474,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": "India <u>1.46 billion</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.523,
            0.292,
            0.633,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": "Bangladesh <u>175 million</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.682,
            0.292,
            0.788,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": "USA <u>347 million</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.354,
            0.212,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>13%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.25,
            0.354,
            0.284,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>8%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.323,
            0.354,
            0.366,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>18%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.354,
            0.444,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>10%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.483,
            0.354,
            0.517,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>1%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.555,
            0.354,
            0.599,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>35%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.638,
            0.354,
            0.671,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>2%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.715,
            0.354,
            0.75,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>2%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.784,
            0.354,
            0.834,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "<u>0.1%</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.392,
            0.846,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": "3. The price of a mobile phone is ₹8,250. A GST of 18% is added to the price. Which of the following gives the final price of the phone including the GST?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.216,
            0.452,
            0.346,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "(i) 8250 + 18"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.527,
            0.452,
            0.686,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": "(ii) 8250 + 1800"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.478,
            0.357,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $8 2 5 0 \\pm \\frac { 1 8 } { 1 0 0 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.523,
            0.483,
            0.666,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "(iv) 8250 × 18"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.508,
            0.361,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "(v) $8 2 5 0 \\times 1 . 1 8$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.523,
            0.507,
            0.747,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "(vi) 8250 + 8250 × 0.18"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.531,
            0.347,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "(vii) $1 . 8 \\times 8 2 5 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.562,
            0.847,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": "4. The monthly percentage change in population (compared to the previous month) of mice in a lab is given: Month 1 change was +5%, Month 2 change was –2%, and Month 3 change was –3%. Which of the following statement(s) are true? The initial population is p ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.64,
            0.827,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "(i) The population after three months was $p \\times 0 . 0 5 \\times 0 . 0 2 \\times 0 . 0 3 .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.665,
            0.827,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "(ii) The population after three months was $p \\times 1 . 0 5 \\times 0 . 9 8 \\times 0 . 9 7 .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.688,
            0.825,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "(iii) The population after three months was $p + 0 . 0 5 - 0 . 0 2 - 0 . 0 3 .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.713,
            0.646,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": "(iv) The population after three months was p."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.736,
            0.75,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": "(v) The population after three months was more than p."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.761,
            0.737,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "(vi) The population after three months was less than p."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.784,
            0.847,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": "5. A shopkeeper initially set the price of a product with a 35% profit margin. Due to poor sales, he decided to offer a 30% discount on the selling price. Will he make a profit or a loss? Give reasons for your answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.869,
            0.846,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": "6. What percentage of area is occupied by the region marked ‘E’ in the figure?"
